repository-code: "https://github.com/sr-dash/heliofield"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  HelioField is a web tool that shows the Sun's coronal magnetic field in 3D
  for any date since May 2010: PFSS field lines from NSO/GONG and SDO/HMI
  magnetograms, the source surface and its neutral line, the heliospheric
  current sheet, and the Parker-spiral magnetic connection of planets and
  spacecraft. Recent days are computed nightly; earlier dates are computed in
  the browser from HMI Carrington-rotation maps.
keywords:
  - heliophysics
  - coronal magnetic field
  - PFSS
  - heliospheric current sheet
  - magnetic connectivity
  - Parker spiral
